proof.text:
Put $R=\Lambda_{X,\Et}$, $S=\Lambda_X=
u_X^*R$, and $F=
u_X^*$. By [det-pe-classical-sheaves-modules], $F:\operatorname{Mod}(R)	o\operatorname{Mod}(S)$ is exact and fully faithful for this discrete commutative ring, and comes from the geometric comparison morphism [def-weil-pbc-site-comparison-morphism]. Regard that morphism as a ringed-topos morphism with structural map $
u_X^{-1}R\xrightarrow{1}S$. Its module pullback is $S\otimes_{
u_X^{-1}R}
u_X^{-1}(-)=F$. Thus [lem-weil-pbc-ringed-topos-flat-module-pullback] says that $F$ preserves flat module sheaves. All sites are taken small in the common larger universe [def-weil-size-convention]. This establishes the blueprint's first paragraph for Noetherian coefficients without applying the finite-ring statement beyond its hypotheses.
